  "text": "To find the least integer \\( k \\) greater than 1 for which \\( b_k \\) is an integer, we need to analyze the given recurrence relation step by step.\n\nWe start with the initial condition:\n\\[ b_1 = 1 \\]\n\nNext, we use the recurrence relation:\n\\[ 2^{b_{n+1} - b_n} - 1 = \\frac{1}{n + \\frac{1}{2}} \\]\n\nRearranging this equation, we get:\n\\[ 2^{b_{n+1} - b_n} = \\frac{1}{n + \\frac{1}{2}} + 1 = \\frac{1}{n + \\frac{1}{2}} + \\frac{n + \\frac{1}{2}}{n + \\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{1 + n + \\frac{1}{2}}{n + \\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{n + \\frac{3}{2}}{n + \\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{2n + 3}{2n + 1} \\]\n\nThus:\n\\[ b_{n+1} - b_n = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{2n + 3}{2n + 1} \\right) \\]\n\nTaking the difference from \\( n = 1 \\) to \\( k \\):\n\\[ b_{k+1} - b_1 = \\sum_{n=1}^k \\left( \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{2n + 3}{2n + 1} \\right) - \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{2n + 1}{2n - 1} \\right) \\right) \\]\n\nSimplifying the log difference:\n\\[ b_{k+1} - b_1 = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{2n + 3}{2n + 1} \\cdot \\frac{2n - 1}{2n + 1} \\right) \\]\n\\[ b_{k+1} - 1 = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{(2n + 3)(2n - 1)}{(2n + 1)^2} \\right) \\]\n\nFor \\( b_{k+1} \\) to be an integer, the argument of the log must be a power of 2. The smallest \\( k \\) for which \\( b_{k+1} \\) is an integer thus needs us to find \\( k \\) such that:\n\\[ \\frac{(2n + 3)(2n - 1)}{(2n + 1)^2} \\]\nis a power of 2. We start with \\( n = 1 \\):\n\nFor \\( n = 1 \\):\n\\[ b_2 - 1 = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{5 \\cdot 3}{3^2} \\right) = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{15}{9} \\right) = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{5}{3} \\right) \\]\n\\[ \\frac{5}{3} \\approx 2.05\\text{ (not a power of 2)} \\]\n\nThus, we increase \\( n \\). Check for \\( n = 2 \\):\n\\[ b_3 - 1 = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{7 \\cdot 5}{17} \\right) = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{35}{17} \\right) \\approx 1.2(11 (non-integral)) \\]\n\nFor \\( n = 4 \\):\n\\[ b_5 - 1 = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{15 \\cdot 13}{57} \\right) = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{195}{57} \\right) = \\log_2 \\left( \\frac{65}{19} \\right) = \\log_2 (3.42)(not powers of 2\\right) \\]\n\nFinally;\nFor \\( n = 5 \\) results in equal.\n\nFinding the smallest \\( k \\), the answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{1} \\]",
